{"title":"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define a sequence recursively by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa5bc43a78deb245bae737e18becd76727e99d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{0}=0,~F_{1}=1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c074b1c5af338ecf311b355847a9aec1b97b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{n}=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a57aecc2a065f288f58c0c367385635a31b3a057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{n-1}+F_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6ef4034e5110b032f729da5b96295b5740f9fd3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> Thus the sequence starts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b788497fdfd1ca7665866d684b2b887a90bf78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,1,1,2,0,2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" /> What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb133b0a0aff76951351275024a47b016473e0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F_{2017}+F_{2018}+F_{2019}+F_{2020}+F_{2021}+F_{2022}+F_{2023}+F_{2024}?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"475\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a7963579276015fe6bd0337f045c9d028e3d4ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"360\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pattern starts to emerge as the function is continued. Note that each next term in the sequence is the sum of the previous two terms mod 3. The repeating pattern of 8 terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/75044d533f6997af5854a40d35ebcca47f63f467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,1,1,2,0,2,2,1\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" /> The problem asks for the sum of eight consecutive terms in the sequence, starting from the 2017th. Since the pattern repeats in cycles of 8, we divide 2017 by 8 and we find that the 2017th term is the same as the remainder, the first term. Thus the sum of the sequence from the 2017th to the 2024th term is the same as the sum of the first eight terms. We now just need to find the sum of the first eight numbers, which is just the same as the cycle noted above. Doing this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d008d8882245f5f2bfca59a6cf940dd1e4c29fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s4vnGlwwHHw\">https://youtu.be/s4vnGlwwHHw</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Y09BGCES_PA\">https://youtu.be/Y09BGCES_PA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A\">2017 AMC 1